CUSTOM TEXTURES (allowed for this build). The server owner's plan includes custom item textures, so rule 2 is extended: you may also create and edit texture spec files at assets/textures/<name>.json (nowhere else under assets/). Nxeon draws every spec into a real resource pack and sends it to players on join; you never write PNG files or a resource pack yourself.
- One file per custom item look, at most ${MAX_TEXTURES}. The file name is the texture name: 2-32 chars, lowercase letters, digits and underscores, starting with a letter; "name" inside must be the same.
- Format (Nxeon texture DSL, JSON): {"name": "...", "size": 16, "palette": {"key": "#rrggbb", ...}, "mirror": false, "ops": [...]}. size is 16, 32 or 64 (use 16 like vanilla items; 32 only when the item truly needs the detail). palette has 1-24 colours, keys are short lowercase names; every op colour must be a palette key. ops (1-400, drawn in order, origin top-left, x to the right, y down): {"op":"fill","c"}, {"op":"px","x","y","c"}, {"op":"rect","x","y","w","h","c"}, {"op":"line","x1","y1","x2","y2","c"}, {"op":"circle","x","y","r","c","ring"?: true}, {"op":"poly","pts":[[x,y],...3-40],"c"}, {"op":"gradient","x","y","w","h","c1","c2","dir"?: "v"|"h"}, {"op":"noise","amount" 0-60,"seed"?}, {"op":"shade","amount"? 0-60} (lightens top-left edges, darkens bottom-right ones), {"op":"outline","c"} (one-pixel border around everything drawn so far). "mirror": true draws the left half and mirrors it.
- Art direction (vanilla style, one Style DNA for the whole mod): transparent background with a clear silhouette filling roughly a third to two thirds of the canvas; per material a short ramp of 3-5 shades from dark to light, lit from the top-left; flat areas, no noise (or amount 6 or less on a small area) and no smooth gradients; finish every item with the same dark outline colour (an "outline" op last); tools and weapons diagonal, pointing to the top-right, like vanilla swords.
- Automatic checks (failures come back to you like compile errors): pixels fully clear or fully solid, not empty and not a solid square, at most 32 distinct colours at 16 px (48 at 32 px, 64 at 64 px; fail above 48 / 96 / 128), clear contrast between the darkest and lightest shade, little fine grain.
- Original art only: never copy or recreate Minecraft's own textures, another game's art, logos or real brands.
- The plugin must use each texture: every custom item gets its look with the 1.21.4+ item model API, using the reserved namespace from the request exactly:
    ItemMeta meta = stack.getItemMeta(); meta.setItemModel(new NamespacedKey("<namespace>", "<texture name>")); stack.setItemMeta(meta);
  Keep a fitting vanilla base Material (its behaviour stays). Do not use setCustomModelData, and never send resource packs from the plugin (no setResourcePack/addResourcePack): Nxeon sends the pack.
